                                                BatteryHealthStatCluster (<-WidgetGaugeHero stats),
                                                loading skeleton, connectivity banner, band->colour
  BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidget.Previews.swift — per-state + per-size #Previews (DEBUG only)
  BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidget.strings        — P1/S10 catalog contribution (table "BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidget")
  BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidget.Tests.swift    — adapter + format + phase + model + telemetry + registry + a11y

File placement matches the CURRENT apps/apple/project.yml: `TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets` is a compiled
source root for the `TeslaSync` (iOS) and `TeslaSync-macOS` targets (`*Tests.swift` excluded), and the
co-located `*Tests.swift` is routed into the `TeslaSyncTests` / `TeslaSync-macOSTests` bundles. This is the
same wiring the committed sibling DriveScoreGaugeWidget (0039) uses. No central registry edit was needed:
the canonical catalogs `WidgetPicker.Catalog.swift` + `MiniGridPreview.Catalog.swift` ALREADY list
`battery-health-analytics` (name "Battery Analytics", category .battery, default 2x4, icon heart.text.square)
— left unmodified (out of allowed scope; referenced by string id only, no compile dependency).

Data binds via the shared P1/S8 `BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidgetSource` seam (the production app wires the
`VehicleStore` active vehicle + the battery-health `Resource` + `SettingsStore`; previews/tests use the
in-memory source). No HTTP in the view. Web hooks reproduced: useVehicles, useBatteryHealthAnalytics
(GET /analytics/battery-health?vehicle_id=), useTranslation, useUnits.

useUnits note (no silent drift, covenant #9): the web source builds a temperature converter from
`unitPrefs.temperature` but never applies it to a rendered value (the tiles are unitless 0-100 scores /
cycle counts / percentages). Native parity therefore renders the raw scores and carries only the number
locale + precision (the real determinants of fmtNumber/fmtInt) in BatteryHealthAnalyticsFormatPrefs.
Documented in the Adapter's BatteryHealthAnalyticsProjector doc comment.

Health bands ported verbatim from the web `scoreColor`: >=80 #10b981 (healthy), >=50 #f59e0b (moderate),
else #ef4444 (degraded); non-finite -> degraded (matches JS NaN comparisons). Gauge centre =
fmtNumber(clamped 0..100, integer->0 / else precision) + "health" unit; below-ring label = fmtInt(soh);
six tiles all integer-formatted (Cycles, Charge Depth %, Discharge %, DC Fast %, Temp Score /100, Habits /100).

States reproduced from the web source (every state renders — no hidden surface):
  loading (skeleton), empty ("No battery health data"), error (retry affordance), stale (chip + retained
  gauge + auto-refresh), offline (chip + cached gauge), content (gauge hero + 6 stat tiles).
isCompact = size.cols <= 1 -> gauge only (no title/icon, no tiles), exactly as the web compact branch.

i18n keys (all from source, resolved through the P1/S10 facade; no English literals in code):
  widget.batteryHealthAnalytics.{title,score,totalCycles,avgChargeDepth,avgDischargeDepth,dcFastRatio,
  tempExposure,chargeHabits,noData} + description; plus native chrome (percentUnit/scoreOutOf/live/stale/
  offline/refresh/retry/loading/emptyHint/errorTitle/staleBanner/offlineBanner) + gaugeA11y template.
  (The 9 web keys already exist as `translation.widget.batteryHealthAnalytics.*` in Localizable.xcstrings.)
Telemetry: `view.opened` with surface slug `BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidget` (P1/S11 seam), emitted once.
Accessibility: VoiceOver label on the gauge + every tile + freshness/refresh/retry controls; Dynamic Type
via tokenized fonts; Reduce Motion respected on the arc + skeleton.

